Cafeteria pre-order system 

Gina Jiang, Krithik Vivekananthan 

PROJECT PROBLEM STATEMENT 

The school cafeteria suffers from long lines during lunch, wasting student break time. The cafeteria staff also struggle to predict daily food demand. There is an opportunity to build a simple, local desktop application where a student can select a meal from a fixed menu, enter their student ID, and submit the order. The cafeteria staff can then see the submitted orders and prepare meals in advance. 

CONCISE DESIGN OVERVIEW 

Components: 

A class containing fields for studentID, selectedItem, and totalPrice 

Input validation for Student ID 

Updating list showing staff the total orders placed during the active session 

Dynamic list storage using ArrayList<> etc.  

Text-based menu loop: a while loop paired with a switch statement that keeps the program running in the console 

SCOPE STATEMENT 

 

What the project includes: 

A text-driven command-line interface in the IDE console 

Use of custom OOP objects to handle data 

Basic text/numerical validation 

What the project excludes: 

Graphic user interfaces 

Permanent data storage 

Multi-user networking 

